Place widescreen draws with fewer vertex scans (the Android branch's
5bcba18, without its tests and notes).

- a draw's screen extent walks each cached vertex run once, keeping the
  last position matrix: it found every cached vertex by walking the runs
  from the first, so a batch of n runs cost n^2/2 steps (a 512-run batch
  231 us on a desktop, 3.6 us now); the bounds are bit-identical (the
  branch's gx_extent_test, 1500 fixtures)
- artwork outside the HUD, and a 3D HUD piece inside a pane, are placed
  without scanning: the offset the scan led to is known beforehand
- the threshold for a camera the game did not widen is worked out once,
  with the widescreen setting

